# Project Rules — trade-note-app (Next.js 14 + App Router + TypeScript)

These rules define the exact development standards, coding conventions, and workflow guidelines 
for the **trade-note-app** project.  
All AI-assisted or automated code generations must strictly follow these rules unless explicitly overridden.

---

## 🧭 Architecture & Routing

- The project uses **Next.js 14 App Router**, located under `src/app`.
- Route groups:
  - Public: `/ (home)`, `/info`
  - Auth required: `/list`, `/mypage`
  - Auth flow: `/(auth)/login`, `/(auth)/register`
- Follow these conventions:
  - Page files → `page.tsx`
  - Loading UI → `loading.tsx`
  - Root layout → `src/app/layout.tsx`
  - Route group folders (e.g., `(auth)`, `(home)`) must not appear in URLs.

---

## 🔐 Authentication & Access Control

- Auth stack: **NextAuth**
- Middleware: `src/middleware.ts`
  - `/list`, `/mypage` → require login (redirect unauthenticated users to `/api/auth/signin`)
  - `/auth/*` → redirect to `/` if user is already logged in
- Required env var: `NEXTAUTH_SECRET`

---

## ⚙️ Server Logic — Route Handlers Only

- All DB, API, and business logic must be inside **App Router Route Handlers**  
  (`src/app/api/.../route.ts`).
- Example structure:
  - `src/app/api/trades/route.ts` (GET/POST)
  - `src/app/api/trades/[id]/route.ts` (GET/PATCH/DELETE)

---

## 🧱 Data Layer — Prisma + @vercel/postgres

- Packages: `@prisma/client`, `prisma`, `@vercel/postgres`
- Schema: `prisma/schema.prisma`
- Scripts:
  - Generate: `npm run prisma:generate`
  - Migrate: `npx prisma migrate dev --name <message>`
- Usage:
  - Use Prisma Client **only on the server** (Route Handlers or Server Components).
  - Database URLs must remain server-only (never exposed to client).

---

## 🧩 TypeScript Rules

- `strict: true`
- Path alias: `@/*` → `./src/*`
- Interfaces use `I` prefix and `Props` suffix (`IUserProps`, `ITradeListProps`, etc.)
- All public APIs (components/hooks/utils) must have explicit types.
- Naming should prioritize semantic clarity over brevity.

---

## 🎨 UI & Styling

- UI Framework: **MUI** (`@mui/material`, `@mui/lab`, `@mui/icons-material`)
- Global theme: `next-themes`
- Style system: **SCSS Modules + Global SCSS** (`src/app/globals.scss`)
- Config:
  - `next.config.js`: `css-loader.modules.localsConvention = 'camelCaseOnly'`
- Rules:
  - SCSS file naming: `*.module.scss`
  - Class names in kebab-case
  - Use camelCase when imported into TS/TSX
- Layout hierarchy: `wrapper > area > box`
  - e.g. `.main-wrapper > .sec01 > .img-area > .text-box`

---

## 🔁 Data Fetching & State Management

- Fetching: `@tanstack/react-query`, `axios`
- Query Keys: array-based (e.g., `['trades', params]`)
- After mutation: invalidate related keys
- Errors:
  - Display user feedback via `react-toastify`
  - Log to console or separate logger

